WEBVTT

00:21:57.359 --> 00:22:00.825
having those dollars go to
law enforcement and safety.

00:22:00.849 --> 00:22:03.191
And I think that opportunity
exists all around us.

00:22:03.215 --> 00:22:06.806
CA: There's been this huge decline
in crime in America

00:22:06.830 --> 00:22:08.166
over the last three decades.

00:22:08.190 --> 00:22:10.170
And part of the narrative of that

00:22:10.194 --> 00:22:14.231
is sometimes that it's about increased
incarceration rates.

00:22:14.255 --> 00:22:16.499
What would you say to someone
who believed that?

00:22:16.523 --> 00:22:20.010
BS: Well, actually, the violent crime rate
has remained relatively stable.

00:22:20.034 --> 00:22:22.684
The great increase
in mass incarceration in this country

00:22:22.708 --> 00:22:24.744
wasn't really in violent crime categories.

00:22:24.768 --> 00:22:26.531
It was this misguided war on drugs.

00:22:26.555 --> 00:22:28.667
That's where the dramatic
increases have come

00:22:28.691 --> 00:22:30.115
in our prison population.